* Shared test bench: the same circuit as xschem/bandgap_tb.sch.
* Every deck includes corner.spice (model library + corner, written by run_all.sh),
* the core subcircuit exported from xschem, and this bench.
.include corner.spice
.include bandgap_core.spice
.param vdd=1.8
.param tr=10u
* DC + AC for op/dc/ac/noise; the PWL ramp from 0 V is used only by the transient start-up test
VSUP VDD 0 DC {vdd} AC 1 PWL(0 0 {tr} {vdd})
x1 VDD 0 VREF bandgap_core
* Hint the DC solver toward the operating state (the start-up test checks it gets there unaided)
.nodeset v(VREF)=1.2
CL VREF 0 1p
